<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="151a" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Mark Paid route and AP export file download</title>
    <phase>6 Export and index (WP6) — wave W6-2 (split from 151, EB-D-181)</phase>
    <gate>startable after 150</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds two routes to the BFF behind the Finance route gate; one moves money-relevant state (Paid is final) and one serves payment files. Tags include bff-api and auth.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Pattern-following: a thin caller of InvoiceLifecycleService (the 104 reject route is the reference) and a download that reuses 090's streaming path; the authorization seam and refusal shapes already exist.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>150</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, ebilling</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the server side of the AP export UI (151 split, EB-D-181): the Mark Paid route (FR-42, Sent to AP to Paid only, through the lifecycle service) and a download of an AP export batch's stored CSV and JSON files. No UI: views, ribbons and the modal are 151b; Email to AP and the settings column are 151c.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF Minimal API, the Finance route gate and the invoice lifecycle service.</role>

  <goal>A caller with the decide right and Read on a Sent to AP invoice marks it Paid in one call; every other status is refused with the lifecycle's own reason code and nothing is written; a caller who can read an AP export batch downloads its stored CSV or JSON, byte for byte as written at export, with the right content type and a filename; anyone else gets the uniform 404.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Read first: projects/ebilling-r1/tasks/151-mark-paid-export-ui.poml (the parent; its Mark Paid goal and criteria apply), decision EB-D-181 in notes/decisions-log.md, notes/150-ap-export-batch.md (the batch, the files it writes as Stored Files with the batch as parent, and the one authorization seam).
      The parent names the Mark Paid route as a SINGLE-invoice route (POST /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId}/mark-paid); this task follows it. The 151b modal calls it once per selected invoice and shows each answer. Existing: no mark-paid route exists (grep "mark-paid|MarkPaid" in src and tests finds none). 090's GET /api/finance/files/{fileId}/content already serves any Stored File to a caller with Read on its parent, but it needs a file id, sends no filename, and serves JSON as application/octet-stream; the batch read (GET /api/finance/export-batches/{batchId}) lists the file ids.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/ApExportEndpoints.cs (two routes; no new endpoint file, so no route-ledger count change)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/ApExportAuthorization.cs (PaymentRouteTargets, beside the export rule: the one seam)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/ApExportService.cs (stable codes and the Mark Paid response record only)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/StoredFileEndpoints.cs (extract 090's open-audit-stream step into an internal helper both routes call; GET /files/{id}/content unchanged)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs (the ApExportEndpoints governed-file text only)</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceRejectReturnEndpoints.cs (route filter, refusal shapes)</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceLifecycleService.cs (TransitionAsync, InvoiceTransitionReasons)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Finance/MarkPaidAuthorizationTests.cs, tests/integration/auth/Finance/ApExportDownloadTests.cs, tests/integration/auth/Finance/ApExportRoutesHost.cs</file>
      <file role="new">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/151a-mark-paid-download.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-42, ADR-002">Mark Paid moves the invoice only through InvoiceLifecycleService.TransitionAsync. Only Sent to AP to Paid succeeds. Every other status, Paid included (a repeat is not a move), is a 409 carrying the lifecycle's own reason code (invoice.transition_not_allowed; also invoice.status_unknown, invoice.concurrent_change) and nothing is written. Paid is never reversed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="EB-D-178, ADR-008">Authorization is the export seam: ApExportAuthorization, the decide right (Write) plus finance.read (Read) on the invoice, asked of Dataverse as the caller, declared on the route. No right, an unknown invoice, a step-0 refusal and a rights-read fault all give the uniform 404 the Finance routes use. The route is in the /api/finance group (step 0, internal callers) and RequireEbillingEnabled follows the authorization filter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-41, 150 notes">The download returns the stored file contents as written at export; it never regenerates the file. A batch that is not Completed advertises no file. Same download pipeline as 090 (scan verdict, own path, audit event, hardening headers).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Stable errorCode on every refusal; a fault is 503 with a retryable message, never a partial answer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 11">Answer the three questions for each new route in the task notes. Extend ApExportEndpoints and the one authorization seam; add no service, no DI registration, no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 10">BFF hygiene: placement statement, publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">No UI. Do not touch the intake files (InvoiceSubmissionService, FromEmailSubmissionService, InvoiceSubmissionEndpoints). Do not edit TASK-INDEX.md, current-task.md or .claude/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add ApExportAuthorization.PaymentRouteTargets (decide plus finance.read on the route's invoice) and map POST /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId}/mark-paid in ApExportEndpoints: a thin call to IInvoiceLifecycleService.TransitionAsync(Paid). 200 { invoiceId, status: "Paid" }; AlreadyInTarget and every Refused reason map to 409 { errorCode: the lifecycle's reason, currentStatus }; NotFound maps to the uniform 404; a fault is 503 ebilling.invoice.payment_unavailable.</step>
    <step order="2">Extract 090's open-audit-stream step into StoredFileEndpoints.StreamServableAsync (internal; optional downloadName). Map GET /api/finance/export-batches/{batchId}/files/{format} (csv or json) in ApExportEndpoints: Read on the batch (uniform 404), the batch read for the file id, the row checked against the batch and purpose, StoredFileService.JudgeServableAsync, then StreamServableAsync as an attachment named ap-export-{batchId}.{format} with text/csv or application/json.</step>
    <step order="3">Update the RouteLevelGate ledger text for ApExportEndpoints (no count change).</step>
    <step order="4">Tests (below), the notes file with the section 11 answers, the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (C:\w151m master, C:\w151b this branch, Compress-Archive, matching file counts, then delete both folders) and the CVE check.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Mark Paid on a Sent to AP invoice by a caller with the decide right and Read: 200 { invoiceId, status "Paid" }; the invoice is Paid (statecode 1) in the store.</criterion>
    <criterion>Mark Paid on an Approved, In Review, Rejected, Returned to Firm, Cancelled or Superseded invoice: 409 invoice.transition_not_allowed with currentStatus, and the stored invoice is unchanged (no write). On an invoice already Paid: the same 409, no write. An unreadable statuscode: 409 invoice.status_unknown.</criterion>
    <criterion>Mark Paid: 401 unauthenticated; no decide right, Write without Read, an unknown invoice, a step-0 refusal and a rights-read fault each give the identical uniform 404 with nothing read or written; 503 ebilling.disabled when the module is off (an unauthorized caller still gets the 404); a lifecycle fault is 503 ebilling.invoice.payment_unavailable.</criterion>
    <criterion>Download: a caller with Read on a Completed batch gets 200 with the stored bytes, equal to what was written at export, text/csv for csv and application/json for json, and Content-Disposition attachment with filename ap-export-{batchId}.{format}; the response never regenerates (a stored file changed after export is served as stored).</criterion>
    <criterion>Download: no Read on the batch, an unknown batch and a step-0 refusal give the identical uniform 404 and no bytes; a format other than csv or json is 400 ebilling.export.invalid_format; a batch with no servable file of that format (not Completed, or json-only) is 404 ebilling.export.file_not_available; a scan-pending file is 409 file_scan_pending; 503 ebilling.disabled when off.</criterion>
    <criterion>The existing GET /api/finance/files/{fileId}/content tests still pass unchanged (the extracted helper preserves them).</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in the task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: the cases above only. Seed-proof the authorization gate once for the route family (disable the decide or the Read check in PaymentRouteTargets, see the tests fail, restore). Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion>Gate: the 5 test projects build; the full ArchTests (ISS-005 flaky, re-run alone, issue 2469), the unit filter ApExport|Finance|Invoice and the integration tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If 150 did not store the export files (only returned them in the create response), STOP: that is a design question for the main session. (It stores them as Stored Files, so this does not apply.)</trigger>
    <trigger>If Mark Paid needs a Decision Record, an approval write or any side effect beyond the status move, STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md section 6).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
</task>
